Migrations


.process of moving data from one system to another 
    .for system upgrades, system consolidation, cloud migration, or adoption of new technologies 
.crucial process due to the changing volumes and complexity of data 
.should be done without sacrificing data integrity 
.critical to maintaining a flexible and effective data infrastructure 
.guarantees that companies can easily adjust to changing surroundings and technology 


.Data migration plan
    .describes the approach and procedures to be taken throughout the data migration process
    .for a good strategy:
        1. Assessment - analyze the quality, quantity, and dependencies of the data as it is currently
        2. Define objectives - clearly state the aims and objectives of the data transfer, including any changes to 
            the system, data consolidation, or technological migration
        3. Data mapping - determine and record how the data pieces in the source and destination systems are mapped 
        4. Data cleansing - clean and verify the data to guarantee correctness and consistency 
        5. Select tools - select the right tools/techniques for loading, transforming, and extracting based on the 
            kind of data and systems involved 
        6. Testing - before the actual migration, carry out comprehensive testing to find and fix any possible 
            problems 
        7. Execution - carry out the migration strategy while keeping an eye on things to make sure everything goes 
            well
        8. Validation - verify the correctness and completeness of the transferred data 
        9. Post-migration support - after the migration, provide assistance to resolve any potential problems 



Types of D.M.
    1. Storage migration 
        .transferring data between various formats or storage systems, sometimes requiring hardware changes 
    2. Data migration 
        .between the various DBMS or versions 
    3. Cloud migration 
        .data transfer between multiple cloud providers or from on-premises systems to cloud-based platforms 
    4. Application migration 
        .moving data from one app to another 
    5. Business process migration 
        .modifying the underlying data structure as a component of a larger endeavor to reengineer b/s processes 
    6. Platform migration 
        .transferring data across several technological platforms, such as switching between operating systems 

    

Challenges to D.M.
    .data quality assurance 
        .ensuring data correctness and consistency during the process
    .downtime 
        .reducing downtime to prevent operational disturbances in the company
    .compatibility concerns 
        .addressing compatibility concerns between source and destination sytems 
    .security concerns 
        .safeguarding private information when migrating 



Steps in D.M.
1. Assessment - determine the objectives of the migration, assess the available data, and make appropriate plans
2. Data profiling - recognize the links, trends, and quality of data 
3. Data cleaning - to enhance quality, clean, and preprocess data 
4. Mapping - establish mapping specifications for data conversion
5. Testing - to guarantee correctness and system compatibility, carry out extensive testing 
6. Execution - carry out the migration strategy ASAP
7. Validation - check the completeness and integrity of the data after migration
8. Optimization - adjust the system to run as efficiently as possible 



